Subject: [PATCH] arm64: qcom: match Liuqin WCN6855 boot and retention votes

The M81 downstream RPMh regulators cache millivolt initial requests. BT
and CNSS then vote their own ranges before enabling shared supplies,
including the antenna switch. CNSS drops its bootstrap floors after FW
init; the production Bluetooth HAL requests retention after UART setup.
Neither uses the three initial voltages as permanent regulator floors.

Model those consumers independently of the shared PMU enable counts.
Pass firmware handoff to the powered target under the sequencer lock,
including PCI enumeration and warm starts. Scope the millivolt VRM
request domain to opted-in Liuqin rails and retain board constraints.

OEM: Xiaomi M81 OS2.0.6.0.VMYCNXM, Cape DTB in vendor_boot.img and
     vendor_a/lib64/hw/android.hardware.bluetooth@1.0-impl-qti.so
     (UartController::Init() requests retention after setup).
     MiCode/kernel_devicetree 1c507816ba8aa6117dcec41f577ef7a66d2091f7,
     qcom/cape.dtsi, lists the BT and WLAN supply ranges.
     MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource eb49e10028e27fa98856cb5e458c0f0ec5b4554e,
     drivers/regulator/rpmh-regulator.c, drivers/bluetooth/btpower.c and
     drivers/net/wireless/cnss2/{power,main}.c implement the voltage votes
     and their firmware handoff.

